<!--
  Merge into ios/ApexPOBClock/Info.plist.

  The usage strings are what the employee reads in the permission prompt, so
  they say plainly what is collected and when. Vague wording here is both an
  App Review risk and the reason staff refuse the permission.
-->
<key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
<string>Apex Clock checks that you are at your warehouse when you clock in or out. Your location is only read at that moment, never in the background.</string>

<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
<string>Apex Clock takes a photo when you clock in so your supervisor can confirm it is you.</string>

<!--
  NSLocationAlwaysAndWhenInUseUsageDescription is deliberately omitted: the app
  never requests background location.

  App Attest also requires the App Attest capability on the App ID and the
  com.apple.developer.devicecheck.appattest-environment entitlement.
-->
